2026-09-27T09:10:31.6465564Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T09:10:31.6466065Z ================
2026-09-27T09:10:31.6466325Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:31.6466664Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T09:10:31.6467376Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T09:10:31.6467824Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:31.6468053Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T09:10:31.6468623Z ====================================
2026-09-27T09:10:31.6469178Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:31.6469425Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T09:10:31.6470237Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T09:10:31.6471003Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T09:10:31.6472338Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T09:10:31.6473363Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:31.6473605Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T09:10:31.6474463Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T09:10:31.6475567Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T09:10:31.6476126Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:31.6476694Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T09:10:31.6477494Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:31.6477759Z Packages
2026-09-27T09:10:31.6478207Z ========
2026-09-27T09:10:31.6478418Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:31.6481455Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T09:10:31.6484267Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:31.6484783Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T09:10:31.6485795Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T09:10:31.6487507Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T09:10:31.6488723Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T09:10:31.6490155Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T09:10:31.6491025Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T09:10:31.6491682Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:31.6491921Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T09:10:31.6492452Z ==========================
2026-09-27T09:10:31.6492805Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:31.6494791Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T09:10:31.6496059Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:31.6496802Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T09:10:31.6497740Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T09:10:31.6497983Z 
